{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011Cgr592bTU3RdiAA2YyS5w","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I couldn't confirm the defect from the snippets, because none of them contain the faulty line. The DTOs, domain model, schema and entity all declare `firstName` and `lastName` separately. The social login services also map them correctly. The path below is my inference from how the boilerplate normally wires registration and profile update, not something I could check here.\n\nBoth registration and profile update end in the persistence mappers' `toPersistence`. That is the only code both flows share, and it is where `lastName` most likely takes the value of `firstName`. I couldn't see either mapper, so the line ranges are estimates. I put `AuthService.register` third because it would only explain the registration half of the report."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0,"cache_read_input_tokens":5054,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":3,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"f87c3b58-7b1e-468b-8e52-f32fe5823b83","uuid":"80006663-8013-4e57-b2ba-7918b24103ad","timestamp":"2026-11-08T20:13:25.103Z","request_id":"req_011Cgr592QZ7FxfKD1WTMuRi"}
